>> mo'e      MOhE     sumti to operand
>> convert sumti to mex operand;
>> sample use in story arithmetic: [3 apples] + [3 apples] = what

This suggests to me that {mo'e de} means "at least one de", where
{de} could be apples, for example.

Which one is right? If {mo'e de} means "some number de", then I can't
imagine what {mo'e pa plise} could mean.

